  "Times and deadlines are Nat; the challenge flag is a Bool; n is a ghost counter of the challenges started while the batch is pending, never read by an action's guard or by another register's effect.",
  "challenge has no guard: unlike Rollup.sol's challengeState, which needs no challenge open, the toy lets a second challenge extend the deadline again. Every challenge then adds W from every state, so the intent contract's L_weak is a claim about every reachable state with no premise."
 ],
